{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer","id":886428,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Occult : The Sorcerer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-09T10:44:40-07:00","id":886428,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Occult : The Sorcerer","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OCCULT : THE SORCERER</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">THE SCRIPTURE OF THE MAIDEN IN CHAINS</span></span></b><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Once, there was a maiden\u2026</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u2026and before her came all the peoples of Creation, and knelt.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They set aside their petty squabbles in her name.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They acclaimed her with many shouts.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They prayed for her safety and her weal.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Not one of them struck free her chains.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cTo know the world\u2026\u201d</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201c\u2026is to own it,\u201d she said.</i></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer is the Exalt, the god, the geomancer and the talisman maker. In the ascending aspect, those under its domain practice artifice, sorcery, thaumaturgy and geomancy. In the descending aspect, they summon demons, worship the Yozis and practice necromancy. The Sorcerer is the constellation of tasks accomplished through use of Essence.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trappings</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer is one of the Exalted and a Prince of the Earth. He displays goods of the magical materials, a caste mark and regal bearing. He wears armor and carries a daiklave.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correlations</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humanity, geomancy, artifice, demon summoning and infernalism, talismans, Essence use, egotism, Yozi-slaves</span></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ThXuoHu.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Resplendent Destiny of the Sorcerer</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (10m); <b>Mins:</b> Occult 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Create a persona. With a repurchase, add (Essence) non-charm dice to any social influence action taken with humans who are unExalted.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Mark of Exaltation</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Within the light of the Sidereal's anima, dematerialized spirits are revealed, appearing as translucent but present individuals who can be seen and heard, although still not touched.<br /> At Glowing, this reveals spirits out to Short range; at Burning, it reveals them to Medium range; at Bonfire, it reveals them to Long range.<br /> When her anima reaches Bonfire, spirits possessing a host are also revealed as shadowy figures above and around their victim.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Invincible Essence Core</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Design, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> It is by the Sorcerer's will that her destiny is set, and none may gainsay her. When she is struck by a reality altering or fate weaving effect, she may activate Invincible Essence Core to completely suppress the change as long as the motes remain committed.<br /> By using Invincible Essence Core, the Sidereal also ensures that there exists a means for her to undo the curse she holds at bay, which is achievable within a reasonable timeframe. The curative may not be easy to acquire, but it is possible. If the Sidereal releases the commitment upon Invincible Essence Core before the solution is enacted, the deleterious effects take hold immediately.<br /> The Sidereal can hold any number of such effects at bay, each it's own invocation of Invincible Essence Core caging them.<br /> While she maintains Invincible Essence Core, those who spy the Sidereal's horoscope can see the hostile fate held in abeyance.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Crafting Arts</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> By the craft of the Sorcerer, great works are produced. The Sidereal reduces the difficulty of all Crafting and Sorcerous Projects by 1.<br /> At Occult 5, she may repurchase Crafting Arts. When she does, she reduces the cost of making rolls on Superior projects by 1 gold experience point, to a minimum of 3.<br /> At Occult 5 and Essence 3, she may repurchase Crafting Arts for a thrid and final time. When she does, she reduces the cost of making rolls on Superior projects by a total of 2 gold experience points, and the cost of making rolls on Legendary projects by 1 white experience point, to a minimum of 3.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Scent of Bugloss and Catchfly</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> The demon realm bears a distinctive scent, and leaves it's mark upon those whom give it their devotion. Out to Medium range, the Sidereal can smell if anyone has a positive intimacy towards a demon in particular, or demons in general. This does not reveal who has the intimacy, but does provide (Occult) non-charm bonus dice on any Read Intentions roll to discover if someone has such an intimacy.<br /> When she activates Scent of Bugloss and Catchfly, the Sidereal may activate Scent of Cypress and Black Locust or Scent of Holly and Hemp reflexively.<br /> Scent of Bugloss and Catchfly cannot be used in the demon realm.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Scent of Cypress and Black Locust</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> The scent of the Underworld is not easy to forget; those who give undying devotion to the undead bear such with them. Out to Medium range, the Sidereal can smell if anyone has a positive intimacy towards a ghost or other creature of the Underworld in particular, or towards such creatures in general. This will catch the scent of those who engage in ancestor worship, but not simply those who retain fond memories of someone that has passed. This does not reveal who has the intimacy, but does provide (Occult) non-charm bonus dice on any Read Intentions roll to discover if someone has such an intimacy.<br /> When she activates Scent of Cypress and Black Locust, the Sidereal may activate Scent of Bugloss and Catchfly or Scent of Holly and Hemp reflexively.<br /> Scent of Cypress and Black Locust cannot be used in shadowlands or the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Scent of Holly and Hemp</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> There is a unique tang that follows those who labor under sorcerous enchantment, astrological design or comparable reality shifting powers. Out to Medium range, the Sidereal can smell if anyone bears such an enchantment. Scent of Holly and Help does not reveal those enchanted by the charms of the Exalted, nor those who are enchanted of a power of their own design, nor the nature of the enchantment. Scent of Holly and Hemp does not reveal who precisely bears the enchantment, but does provide (Occult) non-charm bonus dice on any Read Intentions or Profile Character roll to discover such.<br /> When she activates Scent of Holly and Hemp, the Sidereal may activate Scent of Bugloss and Catchfly or Scent of Cypress and Black Locust reflexively.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Sublime Artifice</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2sxp / 2gxp / 2wxp; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Salient<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Crafting Arts<br /> <br /> By the toil of the Sorcerer, even her failures herald success. By using Sublime Artifice, the Sidereal gains an additional number of successes on a craft roll equal to the greatest number of failures sharing the same number.<br /> (E.g. if she rolled 1,1,2,3,3,3,3,7,10 she would get two successes from the 10, one success from the 7, and four successes from having rolled four 3s for a total of seven successes)<br /> Invoking Sublime Artifice costs 2 silver experience points for a Major project, 2 gold experience points for a Superior project, or 2 white experience points for a Legendary project.<br /> At Occult 5, Essence 4, the Sidereal purchase Sublime Artifice a second time, to gain additional successes equal to the greatest number of successes sharing the same number as well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Blessings of Heaven</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Crafting Arts<br /> <br /> The Heavens shower glory upon the Sorcerer. When the Sidereal purchases Blessings of Heaven, she gains (Essence) silver craft experience points. She gains these again at the start of each story.<br /> At Occult 4, Essence 2, she may purchase Blessings of Heaven a second time to gain (Essence) gold craft experience points. She gains these again at the start of each story.<br /> At Occult 5, Essence 4, she may purchase Blessings of Heaven a third and final time to gain (Essence) white craft experience points. She gains these again at the start of each story.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Terrestrial Circle Sorcery</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Design<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> -<br /> <br /> The Sidereal steps through the First Circle, and is forever transformed. Upon learning this Charm, she gains the ability to learn and cast spells of the Terrestrial Circle. She also gains one Shaping Ritual (Exalted p. 464) and Terrestrial Circle spell for free. This spell becomes a 'control spell', and may be referenced in the mechanics of other charms, as well as always subtly but permanently altering her destiny as writ in the night sky.<br /> When the Sidereal is in the Destiny of the Sorcerer, she changes one die to a success before rolling any shape sorcery actions. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Innocuous Maneuver</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 2, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> The Sidereal makes a circle of her index finger and thumb, imbuing her anima with the weight of Creation. While she activates Innocuous Maneuver, dematerialized spirits which are revealed by her anima are treated as being material.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Rising and Falling Stars</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> From the moment she was born, the Sidereal is destined to join the ranks of the Chosen. At the moment of her death, the Maidens confer and select a new mortal who will bear their blessing and act as guard and shepherd of destiny at the appointed hour.<br /> So long as she has Rising and Falling Stars committed, the Sidereal is aware of the location and health of every unExalted Sidereal within Creation. If it is active during a Sidereal's Exaltation, they receive an overwhelming sense of satori as their brother comes into his own.<br /> Rising and Falling Stars does not function during Calibration, and does not reveal the location of Sidereals who have drawn their Second Breath, or those who stand outside of Creation's boundaries- such as in the Underworld, within the Demon Realm, or beyond the Bordermarches of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Time Enough</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (3sxp / 3gxp / 3wxp); <b>Mins:</b> Occult 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Salient<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sublime Artifice<br /> <br /> By the life of the Sorcerer, all things become possible in time. Upon purchasing Time Enough, the Sidereal increases the Terminus for crafting projects by 1. Additionally, she may spend 3 silver experience points to add her (Occult) as non-charm dice to crafting rolls.<br /> At Occult 4, Essence 3, she may purchase Time Enough a second time, increasing the Terminus for crafting projects by a total of 2. Additionally, she may spend 3 gold experience points to add her (Occult) as non-charm dice to a Superior Project, or (Occult) non-charm successes to a Major Project.<br /> At Occult 5, Essence 5, she may purchase Time Enough for a third and final time, increasing the Terminus for crafting projects by a total of 3. Additionally, she may spend 3 white experience points to add her (Occult) as non-charm dice to a Legendary Project, or (Occult) non-charm successes to a Superior project.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Unweaving Method</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1a; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Mute, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> The Sidereal plucks the light from her brow and twines it around her fingers, before jabbing into the essence of her victim; striking their core to undo them from the center. Unweaving Method allows the Sidereal to make a hand to hand attack as a gambit with a difficulty of 2.<br /> If the gambit succeeds, she deals (Essence) dice of aggravated damage which ignores hardness and gains double 10s. Against spirits, it instead deals (Essence + Occult) dice of damage. Against demons and spirits of the underworld, reduce her target number for the damage roll to 6.<br /> Once the Unweaving Method has inflicted damage, it cannot be used again in the same scene until the unweaving is completed by the destruction of the damaged individual.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>The Unity of All Things</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Blessings of Heaven<br /> <br /> In all things does the Sorcerer draw inspiration and strength. After purchasing the Unity of All Things, the first time the Sidereal assumes a non-Sidereal Martial Arts form, she gains gold experience points as if she completed a a Major project.<br /> The first time she uses a Sidereal Martial Arts charm, she gains white experience points as if she completed a Superior project with a rating equal to the minimum Essence of the charm (or 1 white experience point for a Sidereal Martial Arts Charm with a minimum Essence of 1).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Terminal Sanction</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Mark of Exaltation<br /> <br /> It is the remit of the Sorcerer to pass judgement upon corrupt divinities, for the Exalted have been given possession of Creation. Withering attacks enhanced by Terminal Sanction may strike dematerialized spirits. <br /> Decisive attacks enhanced by Terminal Sanction may strike dematerialized spirits; spirits struck by such an attack are forced to materialize at no cost, and may neither dematerialize nor flee the scene by means of their powers (although they can attempt to run by more conventional means).<br /> A spirit reduced to incapacitated by a decisive attack enhanced by Terminal Sanction may, at the Sidereal's option, be permanently destroyed, spared and allowed to reincorporate freely (with the knowledge they were spared), or spared and bound to perform a specific task for the next year as specified by the Sidereal upon reincorporation; this last is enforced by an unbreakable Defining Principle to complete the task in question.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Forewarned is Disarmed</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Time Enough<br /> <br /> By the vision of the Sorcerer, nothing happens save as she wills. Once per crafting project, she may undo one Crafting roll. She regains half of all craft experience spent in total, including upon Charm activations. The roll does not count towards the project's Terminus, does not contribute threshold successes towards the goal number, and saves the project from having been botched.<br /> Forewarned is Disarmed may not be used twice upon the same project.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Blood and Breath Invested</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m / sxp, 2m / gxp, 3m / wxp; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Design, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> The Unity of All Things<br /> <br /> By the blood of the Sorcerer are her works completed. She may substitute motes for craft experience; 1 mote per silver craft experience point, 2 motes for gold craft experience point, or 3 motes per white craft experience point. <br /> You may substitute any amount of craft experience in this fashion; however, until the project is completed, if you reclaim these motes, the project immediately fails as though botched. If the Sidereal is killed with motes committed to a project, the project is not botched; it is rather held in abeyance for another to finish her unfinished task.<br /> So long as the motes are committed, the Sidereal's destiny is clearly entangled with the work; those casting her horoscope will have difficulty seeing where the one ends and the other begins.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Celestial Circle Sorcery</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Design<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> The Sidereal steps through the Second Circle, mastering the greatest sorceries available to the Five-score Fellowship. Upon learning this Charm, she gains the ability to learn and cast spells of the Celestial Circle. She also gains a Celestial Circle spell for free. This spell becomes a 'control spell', and may be referenced in the mechanics of other charms, as well as more dramatically altering her destiny as writ in the stars.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>All Craft and Cunning Possessed</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Forewarned is Disarmed<br /> <br /> By the cunning of the Sorcerer are limitations shattered. The Sidereal may use Major project slots to undertake Superior projects of building artifacts or raising Manses. The project itself is still a Superior Project as far as other effects are concerned.<br /> At Essence 5, she may purchase All Craft and Cunning Possessed a second time, allowing her to undertake Legendary projects with a Superior project slot. The project itself is still a Legendary project as far as other effects are concerned.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>My Will Be Done</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Blood and Breath Invested<br /> <br /> In the end, it is not the Sorcerer's time or toil or life that realizes her visions; it is her will and essence forged and beaten into solid form. Into this forging are her glories and her faults, magnified by the greatness of what she seeks to accomplish.<br /> When the Sidereal overcomes the difficulty on a craft roll for a Major project, she gains 1 silver craft experience point per failure rolled. When she overcomes the difficulty on a craft roll for a Superior project, she gains 1 gold craft experience point per failure rolled. When the Sidereal overcomes the difficulty on a craft roll for a Legendary project, she gains 1 white craft experience point per failure rolled.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Willing Assumption of Chains</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp, 1lhl; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Terminal Sanction, Celestial Circle Sorcery, and either All Craft and Cunning Possessed or My Will Be Done<br /> <br /> With Willing Assumption of Chains, the Sidereal is empowered by Heaven to strike bargains with spirits on behalf of herself and Creation. After the oath is struck, she pulls out a prayer strip marked with the Scripture of the Maiden in Chains. She slices the meat of her thumb with the edge of the strip and presses a bloody thumbprint to it. The prayer strip is consumed in a flash of emerald flame, bearing the oath to the vaults of Heaven, where it will be enforced as an Eclipse caste oath.<br /> The Sidereal may only make such bargains between herself and spirits, or to act as a signatory between two or more spirits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:59:15-07:00","id":886577,"title":"","content":"Does your Sidereal craft also have craft stuff? I think its kinda too good if both craft and sorcery stuff are in the same tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","name":"Ramaloke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:23:10-07:00","id":886726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramaloke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886577#post886577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does your Sidereal craft also have craft stuff? I think its kinda too good if both craft and sorcery stuff are in the same tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sanity checks*<br /> <br /> Read the Secret Heart gets you craft experience for fulfilling someone's desires.<br /> Elemental Vision makes it cheaper to build manses, but not any easier.<br /> Excellent Implementation of Objectives increases the amount of craft experience she gets.<br /> Implicit Construction Methodology speeds things up or frees your time up, but doesn't help you craft better.<br /> <br /> Resistance has a couple of charms that help with Crafting when you're in the Destiny of the Mast, but you can't have your Lore high enough to work on Superior projects, so I don't really count them for crafting better.<br /> Two Thousand Hands and Two lets you buy mundane project slots with motes.<br /> The Wisdom of Drudges gets you more craft xp.<br /> <br /> So... pretty much, no.<br /> <br /> If you want to be amazing at getting people what they want, you want Sidereal Craft.<br /> If you want to FORGE THE ONE RING IN THE FIRES OF MOUNT DOOM SO ALL SHALL LOVE YOU AND DESPAIR, you go Occult- because that's the tree about about essence manipulation and Exalted artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:33:27-07:00","id":886734,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I don't like how most of the Secrets charm trees have a bunch of crafting charms. I feel like it dilutes the caste's concept. They seem more like &quot;Fate Twilights&quot; than Oracles. Occult is suppose to be the &quot;smack gods back into their place&quot; charm set for Sidereals. <br /> <br /> Of course I could be sore because I was planning on stealing these charm trees for part two of my quest. Giving my quest character access to all these occult/crafting charms would distort my Chosen of Secrets a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-09-2016, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:40:42-07:00","id":886742,"title":"","content":"Weren't there a couple in your Lore or Investigation or something as well? You might as well merge them, if only so crafting doesn't get absolutely everywhere. Also, consider at least a few basic crafting Charms in Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:00:58-07:00","id":886757,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be that one weirdo that chimes in with 'please put crafting stuff in Craft, where it belongs, and not other abilities.' <br /> <br /> Sidereals' obsession with having weirdly placed charm trees and doing other abilites' stuff in different &quot;thematic&quot; trees needs to be jettisoned ASAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:01:46-07:00","id":886758,"title":"","content":"*sanity checks again*<br /> Craft gets you into destiny crafting (Astrological Projections, via World-Shaping Artistic Vision, Elegant Patterns of Fate and Predestined Destiny Shaping- the last of which is also going to be eating into the craft xp), <br /> Craft lets you know what people *want* and rewards you for fulfilling those desires- but it's not really about making stuff.<br /> <br /> Clockwork Soul Style (Investigation) gets you additional craft xp when creating or repairing mechanical devices or automata.<br /> Talisman-Making Touch (Larceny) lets you make talismans as basic / major projects.<br /> Lazy Works Smart Style (Larceny) lets you craft mundane stuff without actually having to do anything.<br /> <br /> That is literally everything that has the words 'project' or 'craft' in it and has anything to do with crafting that's written. It's *possible a bit more might crop up in the remaining trees- in particular, I'm feeling like there's not a sufficient number of craft xp sinks -but it's not *super* likely, and definitely won't serious increase their artifactory-ness. More likely, they'll be spent doing some other weird damn thing.<br /> <br /> That said, a Chosen of Secrets that wants Willing Assumption of Chains could go Crafting Arts, Blessings of Heaven, The Unity of All Things, Blood and Breath Invested, and My Will Be Done to become an engine of craft xp generation without even trying, which she could then funnel hard into astrological designs via Elegant Patterns of Fate. And if you don't want Willing Assumption of Chains, the entire artifice-crafting section of the tree is segregated- you can get all the 'fuck with spirits' and 'know things' powers in Occult without touching it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:09:24-07:00","id":886764,"title":"","content":"In my opinion Chosen of Secrets shouldn't be the &quot;Crafting Sidereals&quot;. They aren't the ones who would be forging the one ring to rule them all. That is the Twilights.<br /> <br /> Not that I don't think the charms aren't awesome. I just disagree about where you place them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-09-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:18:17-07:00","id":886771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886757#post886757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be that one weirdo that chimes in with 'please put crafting stuff in Craft, where it belongs, and not other abilities.'<br /> <br /> Sidereals' obsession with having weirdly placed charm trees and doing other abilites' stuff in different &quot;thematic&quot; trees needs to be jettisoned ASAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at everyone saying crafting should go in crafts*<br /> <br /> I don't think you're alone there.<br /> <br /> *looks at all the other weird stuff*<br /> <br /> No. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My very first principle when starting this was 'The charm trees are going to eat Astrology, and be based around the Astrological correlations and trappings'<br /> That might not be to your taste- hell, I might very relatively unusual in my preference there!<br /> <br /> And, that said- one of the reasons why these Sidereal charm trees have such a 'choose your own adventure' look to them is to ensure that if someone *wants* to build a straight forward embodiment of the mastery of the human understanding of an ability- they can. It'll be a little harder than doing so as a Solar, but Sidereals *aren't* Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:23:21-07:00","id":886774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886764#post886764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion Chosen of Secrets shouldn't be the &quot;Crafting Sidereals&quot;. They aren't the ones who would be forging the one ring to rule them all. That is the Twilights.<br /> <br /> Not that I don't think the charms aren't awesome. I just disagree about where you place them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with you there- Twillights should 100% be the ones forging the One Ring, not Sidereals- neither Chosen of Secrets nor Chosen of Serenity. (And indeed, by a bunch of simple simulations I've run, maxed out Sidereals still have really shitty chances of finishing Legendary projects. They can finish Artifact 5 projects pretty reliably, it's tremendously more expensive for them than it is for Solars).<br /> <br /> That said, people like making artifacts, and making artifacts fits cleanly in the correlations of the Sorcerer- so the charms to best facilitate doing so fall there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:25:12-07:00","id":886778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886734#post886734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit I don't like how most of the Secrets charm trees have a bunch of crafting charms. I feel like it dilutes the caste's concept. They seem more like &quot;Fate Twilights&quot; than Oracles. Occult is suppose to be the &quot;smack gods back into their place&quot; charm set for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Of course I could be sore because I was planning on stealing these charm trees for part two of my quest. Giving my quest character access to all these occult/crafting charms would distort my Chosen of Secrets a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'm curious about this-<br /> What do you want your Chosen of Secrets character to do that requires, or even strongly incentivizes, them going down the 'Craft Artifacts Better' branch of Occult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:28:13-07:00","id":886780,"title":"","content":"As much as I love Sidereal abilities being interpreted in metaphorical ways by their charm trees, crafting feels a bit odd to place in Secrets. I could see the <span style=\"color:#FFD700\"><i><b>Journey</b></i></span> of a meteorite on it's way to becoming a starmetal grand daiklaive, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i><b>Serenity</b></i></span> leading to the birth of an artifact from an emotional bond, and even <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i><b>Endings</b></i></span> if thought of as a transition between states. But Secrets don't come to mind as easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:34:48-07:00","id":886791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886780#post886780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I love Sidereal abilities being interpreted in metaphorical ways by their charm trees, crafting feels a bit odd to place in Secrets. I could see the <span style=\"color:#FFD700\"><i><b>Journey</b></i></span> of a meteorite on it's way to becoming a starmetal grand daiklaive, <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i><b>Serenity</b></i></span> leading to the birth of an artifact from an emotional bond, and even <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i><b>Endings</b></i></span> if thought of as a transition between states. But Secrets don't come to mind as easily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Journeys can help you find what you need.<br /> Serenity help you know what you need.<br /> Secrets know the *how* of the crafting. They know the secret words and ancient powers to bind into the folding of the steel and jade. They know the subtle art and the gross, the hidden wisdom that underlays the chisel and hammer.<br /> <br /> Secrets drink. And they know things.<br /> <br /> (Actually, it's mostly the Chosen of Serenity that drink)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:55:51-07:00","id":886845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886778#post886778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I'm curious about this-<br /> What do you want your Chosen of Secrets character to do that requires, or even strongly incentivizes, them going down the 'Craft Artifacts Better' branch of Occult?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My quest is rules light. There is no xp or buying charms. Basically, I set an Essence Level for each character and assign them Favored abilities. They get all the charms for their Favored/Caste abilities at their essence level. I can get away with giving the characters all those charms because, Ex2 Sidereals don't have that many charms in the first place. <br /> <br /> In hindsight I probably could just pick and choose the charms I like out of your charm and tell my players nope for anything that doesn't fit the character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (My quest is a weird niche situation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:02:43-07:00","id":886851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886845#post886845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My quest is rules light. There is no xp or buying charms. Basically, I set an Essence Level for each character and assign them Favored abilities. They get all the charms for their Favored/Caste abilities at their essence level. I can get away with giving the characters all those charms because, Ex2 Sidereals don't have that many charms in the first place.<br /> <br /> In hindsight I probably could just pick and choose the charms I like out of your charm and tell my players nope for anything that doesn't fit the character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair enough. I can see where that could generate some dissonance- but yeah, mastering an ability tree for a Sidereal means 'I have mastered the meaning of this constellation' rather than 'I have mastered mortal talent at this thing'- expecting the later is going to lead to some dissonance.<br /> <br /> Best thing will just be to say 'You don't have these four charms, because they don't fit the character'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T06:48:48-07:00","id":887126,"title":"","content":"Of course that brings us back to &quot;I don't think all these Crafting Charms belong in Occult&quot;. Unlike Lore and the Scripture of the Old Thing, there is nothing in Maiden in Chains that leans itself to crafting. When I think of Sorcerer, I don't think Crafter. Those are two different roles with two different rule systems. Twilights combine Crafting and Sorcery; it's a hallmark of thier Solar Caste. They are the tinkers and experimenters that create secrets. Secrets infiltrate and investigate to uncover secrets. There are Oracles who are exceptions (Chejop Kejak has Craft favored), but their caste is not defined by it.<br /> <br /> (I also don't want Chosen of Secrets to become the &quot;Twilight-lite&quot; caste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-10-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:04:04-07:00","id":887135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=887126#post887126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course that brings us back to &quot;I don't think all these Crafting Charms belong in Occult&quot;. Unlike Lore and the Scripture of the Old Thing, there is nothing in Maiden in Chains that leans itself to crafting. When I think of Sorcerer, I don't think Crafter. Those are two different roles with two different rule systems. Twilights combine Crafting and Sorcery; it's a hallmark of thier Solar Caste. They are the tinkers and experimenters that create secrets. Secrets infiltrate and investigate to uncover secrets. There are Oracles who are exceptions (Chejop Kejak has Craft favored), but their caste is not defined by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something upon which I suspect we may simply disagree.<br /> I think back to the Chronicles of Prydain, where the greatest treasures stolen by the dark lord Arawen were neither gold nor silver, but the secrets of forge and loom and wheel.<br /> I think back to Sauraman the White, wisest of the Istari and the one most steeped in Ring-lore, who sought to make a Ring of his own.<br /> I think back to ancient places, when the secrets of creation were closely guarded religious mysteries- literally occulted.<br /> <br /> And I look at the meaning of the Sorcerer; 'In the ascending aspect, those under its domain practice artifice, sorcery, thaumaturgy and geomancy.'<br /> <br /> Sidereal Craft governs bringing things together- most profoundly, the weaves of lives upon the Loom of Destiny via Astrological Projections.<br /> Sidereal Resistance governs tasks accomplished through raw muscle power, which governs most mundane Basic and Major Projects.<br /> Sidereal Occult governs the secrets of artifice and geomancy. Mechanically, this means Superior and Legendary Projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:10:50-07:00","id":887139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=887135#post887135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something upon which I suspect we may simply disagree.<br /> I think back to the Chronicles of Prydain, where the greatest treasures stolen by the dark lord Arawen were neither gold nor silver, but the secrets of forge and loom and wheel.<br /> I think back to Sauraman the White, wisest of the Istari and the one most steeped in Ring-lore, who sought to make a Ring of his own.<br /> I think back to ancient places, when the secrets of creation were closely guarded religious mysteries- literally occulted.<br /> <br /> And I look at the meaning of the Sorcerer; 'In the ascending aspect, those under its domain practice artifice, sorcery, thaumaturgy and geomancy.'<br /> <br /> Sidereal Craft governs bringing things together- most profoundly, the weaves of lives upon the Loom of Destiny via Astrological Projections.<br /> Sidereal Resistance governs tasks accomplished through raw muscle power, which governs most mundane Basic and Major Projects.<br /> Sidereal Occult governs the secrets of artifice and geomancy. Mechanically, this means Superior and Legendary Projects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess we will have to agree to disagree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:15:15-07:00","id":887141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=887139#post887139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess we will have to agree to disagree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:56:11-07:00","id":887817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886771#post886771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *looks at everyone saying crafting should go in crafts*<br /> <br /> I don't think you're alone there.<br /> <br /> *looks at all the other weird stuff*<br /> <br /> No. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My very first principle when starting this was 'The charm trees are going to eat Astrology, and be based around the Astrological correlations and trappings'<br /> That might not be to your taste- hell, I might very relatively unusual in my preference there!<br /> <br /> And, that said- one of the reasons why these Sidereal charm trees have such a 'choose your own adventure' look to them is to ensure that if someone *wants* to build a straight forward embodiment of the mastery of the human understanding of an ability- they can. It'll be a little harder than doing so as a Solar, but Sidereals *aren't* Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> After having played a Sidereal for the first time in a four-year game, I have nothing but contempt for the entire 'story-fit-cool' arrangement of Sidereal stuff as-is. Why on earth would anyone want to play a character that is skilled in certain areas...and end up having to spread that skill into entirely unnecessary things just to do the stuff they should be good at from another Ability? It's utterly ridiculous!<br /> <br /> Still, you seem like you're having fun so more power to you. I've nothing else to say, so I'll bow out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T05:15:11-07:00","id":888078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=887817#post887817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> After having played a Sidereal for the first time in a four-year game, I have nothing but contempt for the entire 'story-fit-cool' arrangement of Sidereal stuff as-is. Why on earth would anyone want to play a character that is skilled in certain areas...and end up having to spread that skill into entirely unnecessary things just to do the stuff they should be good at from another Ability? It's utterly ridiculous!<br /> <br /> Still, you seem like you're having fun so more power to you. I've nothing else to say, so I'll bow out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contempt is a harsh word, and I'm sorry that you feel that way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, if nothing else, maybe Where Fate Has Led will led to other remixes that follow the traditional ability structures more closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:06:23-07:00","id":888211,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me and far too long since reading on the Constelations in sidereal stuff, but the astrological correlations and trappings seem to delve too much of exalts as sorcerers, when it stopped being a Chosen-only club long ago, in 1e even, and too little in them as delvers in lost, outright forbidden or simply mysterious knowledge, purveyors of feats both miraculous or profane that would be monumental if not outright impossible to other less erudite and shapers of the fanciful or fantastic into stark reality.<br /> <br /> Looks like the descriptions call for some bit of tweaking and updating, though YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:20:05-07:00","id":888276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/886428-sidereals-wfhl-occult-the-sorcerer?p=886771#post886771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My very first principle when starting this was 'The charm trees are going to eat Astrology, and be based around the Astrological correlations and trappings'<br /> That might not be to your taste- hell, I might very relatively unusual in my preference there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's mostly why I've been staying out of these threads. In a huge fan of sidereal charms and of sidereal homebrew, but I'm not really a fan of his you've been going about it so I don't think my critique on your themes would do you any good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}